WEBVTT

00:00:02.263 --> 00:00:04.003
♪

00:00:29.551 --> 00:00:32.293
We've arrived in
the Portelo system, Captain.

00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:34.164
Any idea what we're
supposed to be doing?

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:36.732
Starfleet was unusually
tight-lipped on the details.

00:00:36.775 --> 00:00:39.343
The whole mission's classified.

00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:40.562
Take us in.

00:00:42.738 --> 00:00:44.522
MARINER:
I wonder what
the big mystery is.

00:00:44.566 --> 00:00:46.655
Ugh, I hope it's not
a Romulan Neutral Zone thing.

00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:47.830
Spy stuff's so boring.

00:00:47.873 --> 00:00:50.006
-[device trills]
-Uh, ah, ah, man.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.443
Whatever it is, I have to start
with holodeck waste removal.

00:00:52.487 --> 00:00:53.618
-Blech.
-TENDI: I don't know,

00:00:53.662 --> 00:00:54.793
but I can't wait
to find out with you.

00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:56.882
'Sup, ladies? How's science?

00:00:56.926 --> 00:00:59.711
We just catalogued some
pretty cool hydrogen samples.

00:00:59.755 --> 00:01:02.627
Hydrogen is the most common
element in the universe.

00:01:02.671 --> 00:01:04.281
Sweet. See you guys at lunch.

00:01:04.325 --> 00:01:07.023
Boimler, make sure you
shower first. Holodeck duty.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.286
Your odor will be repulsive.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.332
Oh, thank you so much, T'Lyn.

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:12.942
You are welcome.

00:01:16.206 --> 00:01:18.033
-[grunts]
-Oh-ho-ho.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.384
Don't get too used to this kind
of work, Mr. Boimler.

00:01:20.428 --> 00:01:23.344
Promotions are coming up, and
I think you'll be very happy.

00:01:23.387 --> 00:01:25.128
Wait, really? I-I...
[clears throat]

00:01:25.172 --> 00:01:26.999
I'm getting a promotion?

00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:28.740
As long as nothing
goes sideways today,

00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:30.307
you'll be a lieutenant
junior grade.

00:01:30.351 --> 00:01:32.657
-But stuff always goes sideways.
-Relax.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.877
You'd have to screw up in
a historically significant way

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.184
-to mess this one up.
-Okay, yeah.

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:39.621
What are the odds of that?
[laughs] Oh, oh!

00:01:39.664 --> 00:01:40.970
[yelps]

00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:42.493
Uh... [whimpers]

00:01:47.368 --> 00:01:50.283
Approaching
the mystery station, Captain.

00:01:50.327 --> 00:01:52.155
I hope this isn't
a Romulan thing.

00:01:52.199 --> 00:01:54.810
-I hate the Neutral Zone.
-Right? Thank you.

00:01:54.853 --> 00:01:57.247
Sorry for the secrecy, Captain,

00:01:57.291 --> 00:01:59.423
but after all these years,
we finally finished.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.818
[clears throat] Beljo Tweekle,
curator and historian.

00:02:02.861 --> 00:02:05.473
Curator? What, are we
transporting some type of art?

00:02:05.516 --> 00:02:07.344
[scoffs] Perhaps the most
beautiful work of art

00:02:07.388 --> 00:02:08.824
in Starfleet history.

00:02:13.698 --> 00:02:17.006
[gasps] Oh, my God, we get to do
something on Voyager?

00:02:17.049 --> 00:02:20.140
Uh, you know, 'cause, I mean,
Boimler's gonna flip. [chuckles]

00:02:26.363 --> 00:02:28.365
♪

00:02:57.438 --> 00:02:59.440
♪

00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:31.036
♪

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:40.045
FREEMAN:
Captain's log, stardate 58724..

00:03:40.089 --> 00:03:42.091
In a pleasant surprise,
theCerritos has been tasked

00:03:42.134 --> 00:03:45.529
with transporting
the USSVoyager.

00:03:45.573 --> 00:03:48.271
Captain Janeway and her crew
spent seven years

00:03:48.315 --> 00:03:50.404
trying to get home
from the Delta Quadrant,

00:03:50.447 --> 00:03:54.321
and they became Federation
history in the process.

00:03:54.364 --> 00:03:57.019
Since their return,
Voyager has been decommissioned

00:03:57.062 --> 00:04:00.065
and preserved
for future generations.

00:04:00.109 --> 00:04:02.459
Her first stop
is Starfleet Command,

00:04:02.503 --> 00:04:03.939
where she'll spend
some time on the ground

00:04:03.982 --> 00:04:05.506
before being permanently

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:07.029
-stationed in orbit.
-[yelps]

00:04:07.072 --> 00:04:08.813
-[grunts]
-CURATOR: Careful.

00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:10.467
That's a mission-worn uniform.

00:04:10.511 --> 00:04:13.644
My legacy depends on everything
making it to Earth

00:04:13.688 --> 00:04:15.342
in pristine condition.

00:04:15.385 --> 00:04:17.822
Unzak, when he guided
the florkas to their roost.

00:04:17.866 --> 00:04:20.521
Whatever. Just don't
touch anything.

00:04:20.564 --> 00:04:22.479
-Oopsie-doodle.
-CURATOR: What are you doing?

00:04:22.523 --> 00:04:24.612
Just taking a peek
at the bio-neural circuitry.

00:04:24.655 --> 00:04:26.309
One time,
Neelix had this cheese,

00:04:26.353 --> 00:04:27.658
and the bacteria
almost destroyed...

00:04:27.702 --> 00:04:29.791
I know all about
the Neelix cheese.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.619
There's a whole display for it
on Deck Seven.

00:04:31.662 --> 00:04:33.185
Don't open panels.

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:35.013
The ship was damaged by cheese?

00:04:35.057 --> 00:04:37.581
It's Voyager.
[bleep] got freaky.

00:04:39.844 --> 00:04:42.804
Hmm. This ship is outdated
and smells like Borg.

00:04:42.847 --> 00:04:44.545
What about Tuvok?

00:04:44.588 --> 00:04:46.024
You must be excited
to see his quarters.

00:04:46.068 --> 00:04:47.939
Perhaps. Are they austere?

00:04:47.983 --> 00:04:50.942
These boxes are for
a rotating exhibit.

00:04:50.986 --> 00:04:54.598
Store them on the Cerritos,
and please be careful.

00:04:54.642 --> 00:04:57.122
Are you chewing gum?

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.734
TENDI:
Ooh, after this, you want to get

00:04:59.777 --> 00:05:02.127
a head start on tomorrow's
titrations with me?

00:05:02.171 --> 00:05:04.347
[gasps] We can label
the test tubes.

00:05:04.391 --> 00:05:06.306
T'LYN:
I do enjoy an accurate label.

00:05:09.265 --> 00:05:11.920
[air whistling]

00:05:11.963 --> 00:05:13.965
♪

00:05:18.405 --> 00:05:20.755
There we go, all calibrated.

00:05:20.798 --> 00:05:22.887
Hey, Doc, uh, want a ride back?

00:05:22.931 --> 00:05:24.324
[grunts] Beats taking a shuttle.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.675
BILLUPS:
You know, growing up, I had
a dragon named Fiddlesticks.

00:05:27.718 --> 00:05:29.067
He was such a good boy.

00:05:29.111 --> 00:05:30.634
He protected me from
all sorts of affectionate...

00:05:30.678 --> 00:05:32.288
Oh [bleep]. Why is it people

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.595
always have to tell me
about their [bleep] pets?

00:05:34.638 --> 00:05:36.031
Right. Sorry.

00:05:36.074 --> 00:05:37.511
Cerritos,two to beam up.

00:05:37.554 --> 00:05:39.382
LUNDY [over comms]:
Copy, Commander. Energizing.

00:05:40.862 --> 00:05:43.212
-[computer trills]
-Something is wrong, sir.

00:05:43.255 --> 00:05:45.519
-There's only one pattern.
-[gasps]

00:05:45.562 --> 00:05:48.522
[yowls] What the [bleep]?

00:05:48.565 --> 00:05:50.654
Where am I? And, uh...

00:05:50.698 --> 00:05:51.960
who am I?

00:05:52.003 --> 00:05:54.832
Captain, we have a problem.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.756
Something over there caused
Billups and Dr. T'Ana

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.105
to merge in the transporter.

00:06:07.149 --> 00:06:09.630
He's calling himself T'Illups.

00:06:09.673 --> 00:06:12.502
This exact scenario happened
to the Voyagercrew.

00:06:12.546 --> 00:06:15.113
Everything is falling apart!

00:06:15.157 --> 00:06:16.550
No need for panic.

00:06:16.593 --> 00:06:18.639
I'm sure I can deal with
this transporter situation

00:06:18.682 --> 00:06:19.944
-on my own.
-T'ILLUPS: Oh...

00:06:19.988 --> 00:06:22.643
Just send me a copy
of Janeway's logs.

00:06:22.686 --> 00:06:24.035
I'll do whatever she did.

00:06:24.079 --> 00:06:26.211
Sending now. Thank you, Captain.

00:06:30.825 --> 00:06:33.349
She knows Janeway straight up
murdered Tuvix, right?

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.959
Huh? Oh, I-I don't know.

00:06:35.003 --> 00:06:36.657
What? Yes, you do.
You're a know-it-all.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:37.919
Get your head in the game.

00:06:37.962 --> 00:06:39.747
This is a historically
significant mission.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.139
It's Voy,man.

00:06:41.183 --> 00:06:43.011
I mean, it's not that
historically significant.

00:06:43.054 --> 00:06:44.621
What? Yes, it is.

00:06:44.665 --> 00:06:46.623
[groans] I'm gonna make sure
going to warp

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.233
didn't knock anything over.

00:06:48.277 --> 00:06:50.018
We've got inertial dampeners.
I'm sure everything is fine.

00:06:50.061 --> 00:06:53.238
It won't be fine until
we're on the ground. [yells]

00:06:53.282 --> 00:06:56.111
Relax. They design these things
to survive a photon blast.

00:06:56.154 --> 00:06:58.766
Oops. Uh, let me just... Wait.

00:06:58.808 --> 00:07:01.333
There's something behind
the neural gel. [gasps]

00:07:01.377 --> 00:07:02.509
-[yelping, gasping]
-Somebody phaser it!

00:07:02.552 --> 00:07:03.814
Look out!

00:07:03.858 --> 00:07:05.207
Oh, God, it's on me!

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.338
Ugh, don't let it infect you.

00:07:06.382 --> 00:07:08.297
-Don't shoot.
-Why not?

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.168
It's a Tak Takian macrovirus.

00:07:10.212 --> 00:07:11.474
It must've been dormant.

00:07:11.518 --> 00:07:13.694
Macrovirus?
Is it making me sick?

00:07:13.737 --> 00:07:16.131
Everyone got inoculated
years ago. It can't hurt you.

00:07:16.174 --> 00:07:18.655
But it is perfect
for the museum.

00:07:18.699 --> 00:07:20.918
Good virus.
Just stay right there.

00:07:20.962 --> 00:07:23.530
Temba, his arms wide.

00:07:23.573 --> 00:07:24.661
[gasps]

00:07:26.054 --> 00:07:29.231
They're spraying DNA
on my babies.

00:07:29.274 --> 00:07:31.320
-Don't let them off the bridge.
-Right, um, so...

00:07:31.363 --> 00:07:32.713
Just stand in front of the door.

00:07:34.802 --> 00:07:35.803
[screams]

00:07:37.239 --> 00:07:38.675
-Boimler, are you kidding me?
-Come on, man.

00:07:38.719 --> 00:07:40.590
Shaka, when the walls fell,
Ensign.

00:07:40.634 --> 00:07:43.985
-Sokath, his eyes uncovered.
-I pay attention.

00:07:44.028 --> 00:07:45.856
-[glass shatters]
-[alarm blaring]

00:07:47.205 --> 00:07:48.859
How can you be this distracted
over an empty ship?

00:07:48.903 --> 00:07:51.732
Uh, you know,
Chakotay served here.

00:07:51.775 --> 00:07:54.256
Dude, this is nothing compared
to, you know, that Pike thing

00:07:54.299 --> 00:07:55.823
we aren't supposed
to talk about.

00:07:55.866 --> 00:07:57.868
Let's get these chunky
cold sores under control

00:07:57.912 --> 00:07:59.740
so we can get back
to enjoying this.

00:07:59.783 --> 00:08:01.089
RANSOM:
They're self-replicating again!

00:08:01.132 --> 00:08:02.177
-Mr. Boimler, get out here.
-[gasps]

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.483
This is your fault.

00:08:04.962 --> 00:08:07.095
T'ILLUPS:
I told you,
I feel [bleep] great.

00:08:07.138 --> 00:08:08.923
Here, let me boost the range
on that scanner.

00:08:08.966 --> 00:08:10.925
He's been
symbiogenetically merged

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:12.753
on a subcellular level, Captain.

00:08:12.796 --> 00:08:14.929
It's called being Tuvixed.

00:08:14.972 --> 00:08:16.713
The same thing happened
to Commander Tuvok

00:08:16.757 --> 00:08:17.845
and Neelix back in the '70s.

00:08:17.888 --> 00:08:19.324
They beamed out
with this flower,

00:08:19.368 --> 00:08:21.196
and it caused them
to merge into Tuvix,

00:08:21.239 --> 00:08:23.415
a combination of
their DNA and memories.

00:08:23.459 --> 00:08:25.853
[gasps] That orchid was in
one of the boxes we moved.

00:08:25.896 --> 00:08:27.811
It must've gotten
into the transporter.

00:08:27.855 --> 00:08:30.379
And that's how T'Illups
was born.

00:08:30.422 --> 00:08:33.730
Captain, I caution against
socializing with the organism.

00:08:33.774 --> 00:08:36.298
Organism? [scoffs] I'm a totally
unique sentient being.

00:08:36.341 --> 00:08:37.647
Plus, I'm cool as [bleep].

00:08:37.691 --> 00:08:39.126
We're gonna be
best friends fast.

00:08:39.169 --> 00:08:41.259
Yeah, T'Lyn, it doesn't hurt
to be friendly,

00:08:41.303 --> 00:08:43.740
since Mr. T'Illups didn't ask
to be created.

00:08:43.784 --> 00:08:45.002
Sure didn't, but here I am.

00:08:45.046 --> 00:08:47.352
I love being alive.

00:08:47.396 --> 00:08:49.659
Well, I'm sure that Janeway
had a solution to this.

00:08:49.703 --> 00:08:51.313
[chuckles] I'll be back shortly.

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:55.099
How many physical memories

00:08:55.143 --> 00:08:57.449
do you have from before?

00:08:59.495 --> 00:09:01.802
[gasping, whimpering]

00:09:01.845 --> 00:09:03.412
Don't let them touch
the exhibits!

00:09:03.455 --> 00:09:04.848
No!

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.459
[computer trills]

00:09:07.503 --> 00:09:09.636
COMPUTER:
Initiating programs Chaotica,

00:09:09.679 --> 00:09:11.333
Clown and Michael Sullivan.

00:09:11.376 --> 00:09:13.857
Safety protocols set to random.

00:09:13.901 --> 00:09:16.120
Random? No.
Computer, set them to safety.

00:09:16.164 --> 00:09:19.254
-Ooh. [laughs]
-Surrender now,

00:09:19.297 --> 00:09:21.952
or face the wrath of Chaotica.

00:09:21.996 --> 00:09:23.824
[panting, whimpering]

00:09:23.867 --> 00:09:25.477
These are, like,
Voy'sdeepest cuts.

00:09:25.521 --> 00:09:27.436
Not as deep as my cuts. Yah!

00:09:27.479 --> 00:09:29.264
-[laughs]
-[grunts]

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:33.050
[grunts] How are these guys
even getting off the holodeck?

00:09:33.094 --> 00:09:35.270
I installed holo-emitters
all over the ship.

00:09:35.313 --> 00:09:37.141
I thought you were preserving,
not adding.

00:09:37.185 --> 00:09:39.709
Oh, subtle updates that don't
impact historical consistency

00:09:39.753 --> 00:09:42.712
are an acceptable compromise
for conservation.

00:09:42.756 --> 00:09:44.018
Wha... Chaotica isn't subtle,

00:09:44.061 --> 00:09:45.846
and the Clown wasn't even
a holodeck pro...

00:09:45.889 --> 00:09:47.325
[moans]

00:09:47.369 --> 00:09:49.458
I love you, but I can't
be with you.

00:09:49.501 --> 00:09:50.546
Ooh, I like this guy, though.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.809
[Clown laughing]

00:09:52.853 --> 00:09:54.115
-[panting]
-[others gasp]

00:09:54.158 --> 00:09:56.247
-Watch out! The Borg display!
-I got it!

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.640
[screams]

00:09:59.337 --> 00:10:00.425
[whimpers, screams]

00:10:02.427 --> 00:10:03.907
That promotion
is starting to seem

00:10:03.951 --> 00:10:06.127
a little less likely,
Mr. Boimler.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:08.303
-[sighs]
-[curator screaming]

00:10:13.264 --> 00:10:14.831
Did Janeway figure it out?

00:10:14.875 --> 00:10:16.877
No, she just murdered him.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.269
[stammers]
There has to be more to it.

00:10:18.313 --> 00:10:20.837
She isolated the genomes
and split 'em up.

00:10:20.881 --> 00:10:22.273
He begged her to live.

00:10:22.317 --> 00:10:25.015
Holy [bleep].
Janeway didn't mess around.

00:10:25.059 --> 00:10:26.887
[sighs]
I don't want to kill the guy.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.410
I mean, he didn't do
anything wrong.

00:10:28.453 --> 00:10:30.368
We aren't stranded
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:10:30.412 --> 00:10:32.283
We could take him to Earth
and get some help.

00:10:32.327 --> 00:10:34.024
Good call. Let's hurry.

00:10:34.068 --> 00:10:36.766
Captain, do you think Dr. T'Ana
will be okay?

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:38.986
[sighs] I think so,
but it didn't take us long

00:10:39.029 --> 00:10:40.857
to look up Janeway's solution.

00:10:40.901 --> 00:10:43.294
Let's just hope Mr. T'Illups
doesn't do the same.

00:10:43.338 --> 00:10:45.557
Are you [bleep] kidding me?

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:55.176
Dr. Migleemo,
I need your help, uh,

00:10:55.219 --> 00:10:56.917
processing my existence.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.396
MIGLEEMO [over comms]:
Oh, what a dream.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.138
Don't do any self-care
until I get there.

00:11:01.182 --> 00:11:03.837
CURATOR:
Help! [screams] Help!

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.230
I can feel it trying
to regenerate me.

00:11:06.274 --> 00:11:08.580
Uh, maybe if I cut power,
we can... [screams]

00:11:08.624 --> 00:11:09.973
Stop helping, Ensign Boimler.

00:11:10.017 --> 00:11:11.540
Why don't you take a break.

00:11:11.583 --> 00:11:12.889
[grunting]

00:11:14.543 --> 00:11:17.198
The alcove's activated. Look.

00:11:17.241 --> 00:11:19.635
MARINER:
What the hell is that?

00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:22.159
RUTHERFORD:
It's a Borg nanite.
We must have missed one.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:25.075
BOIMLER:
It's supposed to be microscopic.

00:11:25.119 --> 00:11:27.077
It must have assimilated
to the macrovirus.

00:11:27.121 --> 00:11:29.079
RANSOM:
It's a macro-nanite?

00:11:29.123 --> 00:11:31.734
-[Clowns laughing]
-Congratulations.

00:11:31.778 --> 00:11:33.736
You've won more Clowns.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:35.390
I can't resist your touch.

00:11:35.433 --> 00:11:36.739
-Let me hold you.
-Computer!

00:11:36.783 --> 00:11:37.914
Delete this guy.
Come on, computer.

00:11:37.958 --> 00:11:40.917
-[laughing]
-[screams]

00:11:40.961 --> 00:11:42.440
[whimpers]

00:11:45.182 --> 00:11:48.055
We just want to talk,
Mr. T'Illups.

00:11:48.098 --> 00:11:49.839
T'ILLUPS:
I don't think so.
You're gonna kill me.

00:11:49.883 --> 00:11:52.973
I promise you
I'm not killing anyone,

00:11:53.016 --> 00:11:54.322
but I am coming in.

00:11:54.365 --> 00:11:55.845
T'ILLUPS:
Help!

00:11:55.889 --> 00:11:57.064
She's trying to kill me!

00:11:57.107 --> 00:11:58.630
We're going to figure this out.

00:11:58.674 --> 00:12:01.024
What? I can't hear you.

00:12:01.068 --> 00:12:03.940
The Cerritosisn't stuck
in the Delta Quadrant,

00:12:03.984 --> 00:12:05.855
and Starfleet has
the best doctors in the...

00:12:05.899 --> 00:12:07.335
I know how this goes down.

00:12:07.378 --> 00:12:10.425
-[both gasp]
-Which is why I need allies.

00:12:10.468 --> 00:12:12.035
[Freeman and Shaxs gasp]

00:12:12.079 --> 00:12:13.341
FREEMAN:
No, wait!

00:12:13.384 --> 00:12:14.429
[screams]

00:12:14.472 --> 00:12:19.434
Behold, Captain Dr. Frigleeman.

00:12:19.477 --> 00:12:22.785
Bring me more scrumptious
senior staff.

00:12:22.829 --> 00:12:25.005
That's an order.

00:12:25.048 --> 00:12:25.832
No!

00:12:26.876 --> 00:12:29.400
Water, room temperature.

00:12:29.444 --> 00:12:32.316
So, you're really okay
with killing T'Illups?

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.972
I am here to hydrate, not debate
on an anomaly's agency.

00:12:36.016 --> 00:12:38.192
Well, I don't know.
I just don't think it's ethical

00:12:38.235 --> 00:12:40.281
to end someone's life
to get our friends back.

00:12:40.324 --> 00:12:42.370
I hardly know
anyone here at all.

00:12:42.413 --> 00:12:44.720
-I am impartial.
-But we're friends.

00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:46.287
[chuckles] Right?

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.679
-[weapon fires]
-[gasps]

00:12:47.723 --> 00:12:50.987
-[people screaming]
-The bartender.

00:12:51.031 --> 00:12:52.423
Tuvix him with Lundy.

00:12:52.467 --> 00:12:53.990
[gasps]

00:12:54.034 --> 00:12:55.644
[people screaming]

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.560
[door whooshes open]

00:12:58.603 --> 00:13:01.041
TENDI:
He's making more hybrids.

00:13:01.084 --> 00:13:03.304
That appears to be
an accurate assessment.

00:13:05.349 --> 00:13:06.742
[grunts]

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:10.224
My career is ruined!

00:13:10.267 --> 00:13:12.269
[crying]

00:13:18.406 --> 00:13:20.974
[groans] Some of this stuff
got in my mouth.

00:13:21.017 --> 00:13:22.976
I'm getting you out of here.
Just hang tight.

00:13:23.019 --> 00:13:25.021
Dude, you don't need me.

00:13:25.065 --> 00:13:27.284
Did Chaotica's ray gun steal all
your confidence or something?

00:13:27.328 --> 00:13:28.633
No, I'm just... [sighs]

00:13:28.677 --> 00:13:30.026
-I'm having an off day.
-Ugh!

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.072
This was supposed to be fun,
and you ruined it.

00:13:32.115 --> 00:13:34.378
-Voyager'sjust a ship, man.
-[sighs] It's not that.

00:13:34.422 --> 00:13:35.640
[sighs]

00:13:35.684 --> 00:13:37.338
Ransom was gonna
promote me today,

00:13:37.381 --> 00:13:39.079
but I don't want it.

00:13:39.122 --> 00:13:40.210
What are you talking about?

00:13:40.254 --> 00:13:41.342
Did you eat some
of that virus slime?

00:13:41.385 --> 00:13:43.387
I'm worried it'll be
like the Titan.

00:13:43.431 --> 00:13:45.694
It took us months
to repair our friendship.

00:13:45.737 --> 00:13:47.304
I... I can't do that again.

00:13:47.348 --> 00:13:49.219
[scoffs] This is a totally
different situation.

00:13:49.263 --> 00:13:51.526
It's not just that.
I should've believed you

00:13:51.569 --> 00:13:53.528
when the captain sent you
to Starbase 80.

00:13:53.571 --> 00:13:56.183
I have bad judgment.
I-I don't deserve a promotion.

00:13:56.226 --> 00:13:58.489
[laughs] You adorable idiot.

00:13:58.533 --> 00:14:00.665
I'm the one who told Ransom
to promote you.

00:14:00.709 --> 00:14:02.145
-You did?
-Yes.

00:14:02.189 --> 00:14:04.452
I was just keeping my mouth shut
so it'd be a surprise.

00:14:04.495 --> 00:14:05.583
You aren't mad at me?

00:14:05.627 --> 00:14:07.411
No. Look, I am really touched,

00:14:07.455 --> 00:14:08.891
but this is why
we can't keep secrets.

00:14:08.935 --> 00:14:11.067
One of us always ends up
covered in slime.

00:14:11.111 --> 00:14:13.156
Yeah, and it's not coming up.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.942
Would you just go save the ship
already? You don't need me.

00:14:15.985 --> 00:14:18.205
Thanks, Mariner.
I'm glad we're friends.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.338
Ew! Did you just
pat me on the head?

00:14:21.382 --> 00:14:23.079
Yeah, it felt weird to me, too.
I'm sorry.

00:14:27.954 --> 00:14:31.392
You are Chondus,
and you're with friends.

00:14:31.435 --> 00:14:33.046
This is Shabarnes
and Swhale Swhalens.

00:14:33.089 --> 00:14:36.005
He's a combination of Steve
Stevens and Matt the whale.

00:14:36.049 --> 00:14:38.312
I want a fish. [squeaks]

00:14:38.355 --> 00:14:41.837
He's not my best work,
but it matters not.

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:47.147
Soon, the entire [bleep] crew
will be a Tuvix army!

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:47.930
[gasps]

00:14:51.412 --> 00:14:54.284
Prepare to energize.

00:14:55.677 --> 00:14:57.113
We have to do something.

00:14:57.157 --> 00:14:59.420
I am already taking control
of the transporters.

00:14:59.463 --> 00:15:03.076
-You can do that?
-Starfleet systems
are easily circumvented.

00:15:03.119 --> 00:15:04.729
Hey, what are you doing?

00:15:06.688 --> 00:15:08.081
[yowls]

00:15:14.435 --> 00:15:16.263
[gasps]

00:15:16.306 --> 00:15:20.006
You combined all of them
into one big Tuvix-y meatball?

00:15:20.049 --> 00:15:21.355
Perhaps I could still split them

00:15:21.398 --> 00:15:22.878
into their individual
components.

00:15:24.314 --> 00:15:25.533
Why isn't it working?

00:15:25.576 --> 00:15:27.274
I cannot isolate
their genetic signatures.

00:15:27.317 --> 00:15:28.884
There are too many
merged hybrids.

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:30.973
[Tendi gasps]

00:15:37.545 --> 00:15:38.850
COMPUTER:
Confirm new heading.

00:15:38.894 --> 00:15:42.071
Setting a course
to Borg Cube 858779.

00:15:42.115 --> 00:15:43.377
Computer, cancel!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.074
[both laughing]

00:15:51.515 --> 00:15:54.083
[sighs] I miss my wife.

00:15:54.127 --> 00:15:55.432
[door whooshes open]

00:15:55.476 --> 00:15:56.868
RANSOM:
Mr. Boimler.

00:15:56.912 --> 00:15:59.001
Zap this stuff
and get me down from here.

00:15:59.045 --> 00:16:00.524
No time. I need an engineer.

00:16:01.961 --> 00:16:03.136
-[gasps] Ow.
-Sorry.

00:16:03.179 --> 00:16:04.659
Wait! Free us, too!

00:16:04.702 --> 00:16:06.661
If we survive this,
we're having a long talk,

00:16:06.704 --> 00:16:08.445
-Mr. Boim-- Uh...
-[door whooshes open]

00:16:08.489 --> 00:16:09.925
-[door whooshes shut]
-BOIMLER: Okay,

00:16:09.969 --> 00:16:11.013
the macro bots
have locked us out,

00:16:11.057 --> 00:16:12.449
but we need to shut down
main systems.

00:16:12.493 --> 00:16:14.321
Um, um, uh,
we got to break Voyager.

00:16:14.364 --> 00:16:16.453
I got to break Voyager.
Ooh, I have just the thing.

00:16:16.497 --> 00:16:18.151
Yes, I knew you would.

00:16:18.194 --> 00:16:20.414
The method employed by
the Voyager'sEMH can only mark

00:16:20.457 --> 00:16:21.850
one individual.

00:16:21.893 --> 00:16:24.026
High command will not
be impressed with my error.

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:26.202
TENDI:
That scanner T'Illups suggested

00:16:26.246 --> 00:16:29.249
picks up all sorts of stuff,
including personality traits.

00:16:29.292 --> 00:16:31.077
That's how we can fix this.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.340
I fail to see how that helps me
differentiate a whale

00:16:33.383 --> 00:16:34.515
from Steve Stevens.

00:16:34.558 --> 00:16:35.951
Because you don't know them.
Look.

00:16:35.995 --> 00:16:38.606
This area is proud, confident
and a little silly.

00:16:38.649 --> 00:16:39.868
Oh, that's the captain.

00:16:39.911 --> 00:16:41.478
If I isolate genetic code

00:16:41.522 --> 00:16:43.132
and you mark
their personalities...

00:16:43.176 --> 00:16:44.481
We can get everyone back.

00:16:44.525 --> 00:16:45.917
Why are you helping me?

00:16:45.961 --> 00:16:47.832
Do you not have ethical problems
with this solution?

00:16:47.876 --> 00:16:49.660
Well, yeah, I did, but, uh,

00:16:49.704 --> 00:16:51.532
this is a non-sentient
blob of meat,

00:16:51.575 --> 00:16:53.708
so I'm willing to go outside
my comfort zone. [chuckles]

00:16:53.751 --> 00:16:55.188
I mean, for our friends.

00:16:55.231 --> 00:16:57.364
Hmm. Thank you.

00:17:06.286 --> 00:17:07.896
Are you sure this is gonna work?

00:17:07.939 --> 00:17:09.854
Nope, but it feels like
a kooky Voyagersolution,

00:17:09.897 --> 00:17:11.943
-so it's worth a try.
-COMPUTER: Bridge.

00:17:17.862 --> 00:17:20.300
-[screams, grunts]
-CHAOTICA: Any last words

00:17:20.343 --> 00:17:24.173
before you feel the sting
of my electro Luger?

00:17:25.218 --> 00:17:27.394
Ha! There's only one thing

00:17:27.436 --> 00:17:29.918
you haven't thought of,
Dr. Chaotica.

00:17:29.961 --> 00:17:33.748
[laughs] Please, I think
of everything at all times.

00:17:33.791 --> 00:17:36.272
[laughs] That's what you think.

00:17:36.316 --> 00:17:38.187
What are you babbling
about, fool?

00:17:38.231 --> 00:17:40.189
I am not a Starfleet ensign.

00:17:40.233 --> 00:17:43.192
I am the son of Captain Proton.

00:17:43.236 --> 00:17:45.020
[gasps] No.

00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:46.413
[laughs] I got it.

00:17:46.456 --> 00:17:48.632
How could that be-be-be?

00:17:48.676 --> 00:17:50.243
-[glitching continues]
-It's working.

00:17:50.286 --> 00:17:53.115
What the hell is wrong
with you, Chaotica?

00:17:53.159 --> 00:17:56.118
COMPUTER:
Alert. Bio-neural systems
shutting down.

00:17:56.162 --> 00:17:57.424
[glitching]:
Wh-Wh-Wh-What?

00:17:57.467 --> 00:17:58.947
Saints preserve us.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.210
I am full of love.

00:18:01.254 --> 00:18:03.038
Ooh, I'll cut off your head!

00:18:03.082 --> 00:18:05.649
-[screams]
-[glitching laugh]

00:18:05.693 --> 00:18:08.043
Oh, we did it. We broke Voyager.

00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:10.741
What did you do
to my beautiful ship?

00:18:10.785 --> 00:18:12.178
I used the Neelix cheese.

00:18:12.221 --> 00:18:14.049
It gummed up the neural network
just the way it likes.

00:18:14.093 --> 00:18:15.877
[screams]

00:18:17.226 --> 00:18:19.794
[grunts] Let's get
this bad boy locked up.

00:18:19.837 --> 00:18:22.231
We should still have time
to clean before we get to Earth.

00:18:22.275 --> 00:18:24.451
Well done. [groans]

00:18:24.494 --> 00:18:27.976
Now I have to add another
exhibit to the Voyagerstory.

00:18:28.019 --> 00:18:30.761
♪

00:18:43.339 --> 00:18:45.036
FREEMAN:
Captain's log, supplemental.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:48.388
After an embarrassing day

00:18:48.431 --> 00:18:50.303
of being merged
on a subcellular level

00:18:50.346 --> 00:18:52.348
with my senior staff,

00:18:52.392 --> 00:18:54.437
we are putting
the awkwardness behind us

00:18:54.481 --> 00:18:56.352
with a promotion ceremony.

00:18:56.396 --> 00:18:58.659
[clears throat] Today's, uh...

00:18:58.702 --> 00:19:01.923
frankly bizarre series
of Voyagerthemed obstacles

00:19:01.966 --> 00:19:06.362
only prove that you are all
creative, accomplished officers.

00:19:06.406 --> 00:19:10.018
Commander, please announce our
new lieutenant junior grades.

00:19:11.019 --> 00:19:12.542
RANSOM:
Ensign Brad Boimler.

00:19:14.414 --> 00:19:16.416
[others whooping]

00:19:16.459 --> 00:19:17.721
Quick thinking today,
Mr. Boimler.

00:19:17.765 --> 00:19:18.809
Thank you, sir.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:24.293
-Provisional Ensign T'Lyn.
-[others whooping]

00:19:24.337 --> 00:19:27.383
Unexpected, but appreciated.

00:19:27.427 --> 00:19:29.994
-RANSOM: Ensign D'Vana Tendi.
-Oh, my gosh! What? No way!

00:19:30.038 --> 00:19:31.648
[others cheering]

00:19:31.692 --> 00:19:34.564
Thank you, sir.
Guys, I got a pip!

00:19:34.608 --> 00:19:36.697
All right, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:40.309
My main objective here
is to prove to the High Council

00:19:40.353 --> 00:19:42.703
that I should be reinstated
to the Vulcan fleet.

00:19:42.746 --> 00:19:44.487
But after today,

00:19:44.531 --> 00:19:46.881
I have grown to respect
your skills as a scientist.

00:19:46.924 --> 00:19:49.492
I'm so excited
we got promoted together.

00:19:49.536 --> 00:19:52.321
Now we really can be
best science friends.

00:19:52.365 --> 00:19:55.150
That is not the lesson
to take from this moment.

00:19:55.194 --> 00:19:58.458
Damn, looks like half of Beta
shift will be ensigns no more.

00:19:58.501 --> 00:20:00.111
Ooh, let's hit the bar
and celebrate.

00:20:00.155 --> 00:20:02.636
And, finally,
Ensign Beckett Mariner.

00:20:02.679 --> 00:20:04.028
-Wait, wh-what?
-[gasps]

00:20:04.072 --> 00:20:05.465
-[applause]
-[laughs]

00:20:05.508 --> 00:20:07.423
Sir, I...
No, this has to be a mistake.

00:20:07.467 --> 00:20:09.512
Congratulations, Lieutenant.

00:20:14.952 --> 00:20:16.737
-[door chimes]
-Yo, yo.

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:18.391
Sir, this is wrong.

00:20:18.434 --> 00:20:20.044
I don't want to get promoted.

00:20:20.088 --> 00:20:21.481
I know you don't.

00:20:21.524 --> 00:20:24.571
Okay, then stop sliding it
back to me and throw it out.

00:20:24.614 --> 00:20:26.137
Did you know Voyager's
full of cameras?

00:20:26.181 --> 00:20:28.444
Came in handy when putting
together the old mission log.

00:20:28.488 --> 00:20:31.360
I saw you help Boimler
be the best he could be.

00:20:31.404 --> 00:20:32.970
So what? Boimler loves
being encouraged.

00:20:33.014 --> 00:20:34.189
It's, like, his favorite thing.

00:20:34.233 --> 00:20:35.886
I went back and dug
through your record.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.714
You've had a lot of
small-minded commanders

00:20:37.758 --> 00:20:39.586
who promoted then demoted you.

00:20:39.629 --> 00:20:42.371
But now,
you're with Jack Ransom.

00:20:42.415 --> 00:20:44.417
I'm twice as smart
as any of those other guys,

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:47.202
and I know you just need someone
to believe in you.

00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:48.856
Consider yourself lucky

00:20:48.899 --> 00:20:51.206
that you have an amazing
commanding officer.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.382
Sir, I am refusing
this promotion.

00:20:53.426 --> 00:20:55.428
-You can't do this to me.
-No, not gonna hear it.

00:20:55.471 --> 00:20:57.604
-You're dismissed, Lieutenant.
-No, this isn't over.

00:20:57.647 --> 00:20:58.692
I'm not leaving.

00:20:58.735 --> 00:21:00.389
For real.
I-I'm staying right here

00:21:00.433 --> 00:21:02.739
-until you listen to reason.
-[grunts] You do you.

00:21:02.783 --> 00:21:05.176
-[grunts] Feel the burn.
-[groaning]

00:21:10.443 --> 00:21:12.183
-Mm.
-Yeah, I...

00:21:12.227 --> 00:21:14.011
I couldn't even talk him
out of it. He's such an idiot.

00:21:14.055 --> 00:21:15.491
What are you so bummed about?

00:21:15.535 --> 00:21:16.666
Now we get to be
lieutenant JGs together.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.842
[sighs] All of us
except Rutherford.

00:21:18.886 --> 00:21:21.192
I mean, I did break Voyager.

00:21:21.236 --> 00:21:23.064
Engineers can't get promoted
for breaking stuff.

00:21:23.107 --> 00:21:24.500
We always fix things.

00:21:24.544 --> 00:21:26.110
Shouldn't you be drunk
and chanting

00:21:26.154 --> 00:21:27.590
with a fist in the air
right now?

00:21:27.634 --> 00:21:30.550
Come on, no more bunks,
no more holodeck duty!

00:21:30.593 --> 00:21:31.594
We did it!

00:21:31.638 --> 00:21:33.466
I know.
I just, I-I can't believe

00:21:33.509 --> 00:21:35.511
we're not lower decks anymore.

00:21:35.555 --> 00:21:37.165
We're lieutenant junior grades,

00:21:37.208 --> 00:21:39.515
the least important
mid-level officers.

00:21:39.559 --> 00:21:41.038
We do all the grunt work
with none of the perks.

00:21:41.082 --> 00:21:42.431
We're still lower decks.

00:21:42.475 --> 00:21:44.868
Yeah, maybe you're right,
and-and, hey,

00:21:44.912 --> 00:21:47.480
maybe from now on, our lives
will be a lot easier. All right.

00:21:47.523 --> 00:21:48.785
MARINER and BOIMLER:
Lower decks!

00:21:48.829 --> 00:21:50.787
ALL:
Lower decks! Lower decks!

00:21:50.831 --> 00:21:52.354
-Lower decks!
-Come on, T'Lyn.

00:21:52.398 --> 00:21:54.835
Lower decks! Lower decks!

00:21:54.878 --> 00:21:56.402
-[chanting continues]
-TENDI: This is
going to be great!

00:21:56.445 --> 00:21:59.579
New jobs and no mysterious
threats to get in our way.

00:21:59.622 --> 00:22:00.623
GROUP:
No mysterious threats!

00:22:11.678 --> 00:22:12.940
[groans]

00:22:12.983 --> 00:22:15.595
Cease that nervous honing
and let me sleep.

00:22:15.638 --> 00:22:17.727
I am not nervous. I am restless.

00:22:17.771 --> 00:22:20.556
Eager to ram my blade
through my enemies.

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:22.819
That's not a blade.
It's a spear.

00:22:22.863 --> 00:22:25.300
A coward's weapon used
to poke a foe at a distance.

00:22:25.344 --> 00:22:26.780
It has no honor.

00:22:26.823 --> 00:22:30.000
Nobody calls me a coward
and lives to tell the tale.

00:22:30.044 --> 00:22:31.045
[grunts]

00:22:31.088 --> 00:22:33.526
[both grunt]

00:22:33.569 --> 00:22:34.962
Are you free for lunch today?

00:22:35.005 --> 00:22:37.530
They are serving eyes
or hearts or something.

00:22:37.573 --> 00:22:39.183
[sighs] I cannot make it.

00:22:39.227 --> 00:22:42.622
The captain has ordered me
to sit with Commander Vekras

00:22:42.665 --> 00:22:45.320
and transcribe his tedious
battle tales.

00:22:45.364 --> 00:22:46.887
It is a waste of time.

00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:50.194
Ma'ah lucked his way
into that captain's chair.

00:22:50.238 --> 00:22:52.283
He forgets who
his true allies are.

00:22:52.327 --> 00:22:54.764
He won't be captain much longer.

00:22:54.808 --> 00:22:56.418
-[alarm blaring]
-[both gasp]

00:22:56.462 --> 00:22:59.595
We are in battle. Who was wrong
to sharpen their spear now?

00:22:59.639 --> 00:23:00.727
[grunts]

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:02.685
♪

00:23:06.559 --> 00:23:09.257
I read one life sign
on board, Captain.

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:12.260
Unknown vessel, you have drifted
into Klingon space.

00:23:12.303 --> 00:23:13.609
Identify yourself.

00:23:17.221 --> 00:23:19.136
No response.
Should we fire on them?

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:22.662
We gain no honor in destroying
an incapacitated ship.

00:23:22.705 --> 00:23:25.142
Mark their location and resume
our course to Qo'noS.

00:23:25.186 --> 00:23:27.928
Sir, it's moving.

00:23:29.016 --> 00:23:30.452
KEY'LOR:
They're charging weapons.

00:23:30.496 --> 00:23:32.019
Destroy those qoHpu'.

00:23:32.062 --> 00:23:33.977
I said fire.

00:23:34.021 --> 00:23:35.152
I'm trying,
but weapons are down.

00:23:35.196 --> 00:23:36.153
What?

00:23:36.197 --> 00:23:37.720
All systems are losing power.

00:23:37.764 --> 00:23:38.765
That's impossible.

00:23:42.116 --> 00:23:44.031
[all scream]

00:23:58.132 --> 00:24:01.135
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:24:47.268 --> 00:24:48.704
[man imitates weapons firing]

00:24:50.706 --> 00:24:51.707
Chirp.
